Third-party material carried in the nym_auth module
---------------------------------------------------

src/nymauth/lfc2.rs is derived in part from the Rust runtime of Google's longfellow-zk,
https://github.com/google/longfellow-zk at commit 61a8a735964d1b22bccf79bf14ef6767249cdf92:

  rust/core/proto/src/reader/lfc2.rs   (the LFC2 circuit reader and its hardening limits)
  rust/core/proto/src/writer/lfc1.rs   (the LFC1 layout it is converted to)
  rust/core/proto/src/uleb.rs          (ULEB128 reading)

  Copyright 2026 Google LLC. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of the
  licence is in third_party/google-longfellow-zk/LICENSE. The upstream repository has no NOTICE
  file. Modified: ported to this crate's types and error handling, reads into the LFC1 byte
  layout instead of Google's circuit type, with a tighter output budget and an exact two-circuit
  rule. The file keeps the Apache-2.0 notice in its header; Apache-2.0 material in a file covered
  by MPL-2.0 is permitted with these notices kept.

Not derived from Google code, but built to interoperate with it: the nym_auth witness builder,
prover and verifier are written against this crate's own primitives following the SIROS
nym-auth-circuits specification (SPEC.md L3 to L6) and its reference implementation, both
authored by SIROS.

SIROS-supplied data
-------------------

src/nymauth/profiles/ and test-vectors/nymauth/ (circuits, witnesses, credential, verifier request,
proof, slot map) come from the SIROS nym-auth-circuits archive. SIROS owns them and distributes
them here under this repository's licence (MPL-2.0).
